-- COMMAND ----------

-- MAGIC %md-sandbox
-- MAGIC #### B1.2 Tables (Managed or External) with Data on DBFS Mount
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC This scenario involves HMS tables whose data resides in external cloud storage that is mounted on DBFS. This can apply to:
-- MAGIC - **External tables** with a data location that overrides the default
-- MAGIC  external tables
-- MAGIC  - **Managed tables**, where the managed storage location was overridden (for example, at the schema level)
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC These cases are simpler because we don't have to copy data, and there are no subsequent duplicates that we have to manage. We simply:
-- MAGIC - upgrade the DBFS mount by registering the external cloud storage location with Unity Catalog (using a storage credential and external location)
-- MAGIC - create an external table in UC, using the external location
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC <div style="border-left: 4px solid #ff9800; background: #fff3e0; padding: 16px 20px; border-radius: 8px; margin: 16px 0;">
-- MAGIC   <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px;">
-- MAGIC     <span style="font-size: 24px;">⚠️</span>
-- MAGIC     <div>
-- MAGIC       If the HMS table is managed, converting it to external before migration is a good idea. Otherwise, data loss could occur if the original table is dropped.
-- MAGIC     </div>
-- MAGIC   </div>
-- MAGIC </div>
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC <div style="display:flex; justify-content:center;">
