-- COMMAND ----------

-- MAGIC %md-sandbox
-- MAGIC #### B1.4 Recap
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC The upgrade path for any given table will depend on how the source table data is stored, as well as the desired outcome.
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC - External tables, which typically store their data files in external cloud storage can be upgraded using SYNC. This yields an external table in Unity Catalog. This is the least complicated upgrade path to orchestrate, because you don't have to worry about managing changes to the source table data. There's only ever one copy of the data.
-- MAGIC - We can upgrade managed tables the same way, if their data lives in external storage rather than the default DBFS root. But, we should convert the table to external first, to avoid inadvertent data loss if the source table is dropped.
-- MAGIC - For managed HMS tables with data on the DBFS root, the only upgrade option here is rebuilding the table in the Unity Catalog metastore. This results in a managed table. Depending on the format of the source table, you can use clone or CTAS for this. This path results in data movement, as well as two copies of the data to deal with. Ongoing synchronization will be something that has to be considered if legacy workloads continue to modify the source table.
-- MAGIC
