-- MAGIC </div>
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC - **Organization:** With the availability of a three-level namespace, consider how to organize your functions; whether you will collocate them with relevant tables/views, segregate them in a separate schema or catalog, or some hybrid approach.
-- MAGIC - **Two-level references:** Taking organization into account, any two-level references encoded in your function will need to be augmented to include a catalog as well.
-- MAGIC - **Membership tests:** Any references to `is_member()` (which tests membership of a workspace local group) should be changed to `is_account_group_member()`
-- MAGIC - **Dynamic views:** If the function is supporting a dynamic view, consider switching to a more modern approach, such as [Attributed Based Access Control](https://docs.databricks.com/aws/en/data-governance/unity-catalog/abac/) (ABAC) or [per-table row filtering/column masking](https://docs.databricks.com/aws/en/data-governance/unity-catalog/filters-and-masks).
-- MAGIC

-- COMMAND ----------

-- MAGIC %md-sandbox
-- MAGIC ### B3. Views
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Migrating views from HMS UC requires careful attention, as views behave differently across the two systems and there are important limitations and steps to consider. Key considerations include:
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC - **Access Controls:** In Unity Catalog, the owner of a view **does not** need to also own any referenced tables or views. The owner only requires access to those objects (via `SELECT`, `USE SCHEMA`, and `USE CATALOG`). The consumer only needs `SELECT` on the view.
