-- MAGIC UCX provides automated workflows for migrating tables from Hive Metastore to Unity Catalog in Databricks, including managed and external tables. The overall process is as follows:
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC 1. **Bootstrap UCX:** Install and run the UCX installer from an independent compute environment. This will set up configuration metadata and a collection of workflows in the target workspace.
-- MAGIC 1. **Run the Assessment:** The assessment workflow examines the compatibility of your workspace’s groups, storage, access controls, and tables and records this information for your use and by the other UCX utilities.
-- MAGIC 1. **Configure table mapping:** Using the CLI, set up a table mapping file. This will generate a CSV inventory of all the HMS tables. Once generated, you can update the file to omit tables or views from the migration (by removing the record) or adjust where they'll be migrated to by changing the record). For example, the following changes will:
-- MAGIC    - change the destination catalog name from the default (workspace ID) to `sales_dev`
-- MAGIC    - change the schema name from `sales_analysis` to `sales`
-- MAGIC    - change the table name from `ytd_sales` to `ytd_analysis`
-- MAGIC    <table>
-- MAGIC   <thead>
-- MAGIC     <tr>
-- MAGIC       <th>workspace</th>
-- MAGIC       <th>catalog</th>
-- MAGIC       <th>src_schema</th>
-- MAGIC       <th>dst_schema</th>
-- MAGIC       <th>src_table</th>
-- MAGIC       <th>dst_table</th>
-- MAGIC     </tr>
-- MAGIC   </thead>
-- MAGIC   <tbody>
-- MAGIC     <tr>
-- MAGIC       <td>sales_dev</td>
-- MAGIC       <td>123333333</td>
-- MAGIC       <td>sales_analysis</td>
-- MAGIC       <td>sales_analysis</td>
-- MAGIC       <td>ytd_sales</td>
-- MAGIC       <td>ytd_sales</td>
-- MAGIC     </tr>
-- MAGIC     <tr>
-- MAGIC       <td/>
-- MAGIC       <td style="text-align: center;">&#8595;</td>
-- MAGIC       <td/>
-- MAGIC       <td style="text-align: center;">&#8595;</td>
-- MAGIC       <td/>
-- MAGIC       <td style="text-align: center;">&#8595;</td>
-- MAGIC     </tr>
-- MAGIC     <tr>
-- MAGIC       <td>sales_dev</td>
-- MAGIC       <td><strong>sales_dev</strong></td>
-- MAGIC       <td>sales_analysis</td>
-- MAGIC       <td><strong>sales</strong></td>
-- MAGIC       <td>ytd_sales</td>
-- MAGIC       <td><strong>ytd_analysis</strong></td>
-- MAGIC     </tr>
-- MAGIC   </tbody>
-- MAGIC </table>
-- MAGIC 1. **Data access:** Set up external locations using UCX commands, allowing external data to be properly mapped into the UC metastore as needed.
-- MAGIC 1. **Migrate tables:** By running a UCX CLI command (or running the associated workflows directly in the target workspace) actual table migration takes place following the mapping file set up previously.

